</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Theoretical Foundations and Successive Refinement</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Successive Refinement.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The successive refinement problem, introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Equitz &amp; Cover (1991)</a></cite>, asks whether a source can be encoded in stages so that each refinement achieves the same distortion-rate limit as a single-shot encoder. Formally, for target distortions <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}&gt;D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}&gt;D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we seek an encoding system that first represents <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{W}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{W}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> at rate <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with distortion <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then refines this representation to distortion <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> using an additional rate <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}-R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}-R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, without exceeding the total rate <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}=R(D_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}=R(D_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following definition follows this notion.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Successive Refinability of General Sources)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A source is said to be successively refinable from <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists a sequence of encoders</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{n}:\mathcal{W}^{n}\to\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\},\qquad j_{n}:\mathcal{W}^{n}\to\{1,\ldots,2^{\,n(R_{2}-R_{1})}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{n}:\mathcal{W}^{n}\to\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\},\qquad j_{n}:\mathcal{W}^{n}\to\{1,\ldots,2^{\,n(R_{2}-R_{1})}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and respective reconstruction functions (decoders)</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1n}:\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\}\to\widehat{\mathcal{W}}_{1}^{\,n},\qquad g_{2n}:\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\}\times\{1,\ldots,2^{\,n(R_{2}-R_{1})}\}\to\widehat{\mathcal{W}}_{2}^{\,n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1n}:\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\}\to\widehat{\mathcal{W}}_{1}^{\,n},\qquad g_{2n}:\{1,\ldots,2^{nR_{1}}\}\times\{1,\ldots,2^{\,n(R_{2}-R_{1})}\}\to\widehat{\mathcal{W}}_{2}^{\,n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">such that the reconstructions</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{1}^{\,n}=g_{1n}\!\big(i_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n})\big),\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{2}^{\,n}=g_{2n}\!\big(i_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n}),\,j_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{1}^{\,n}=g_{1n}\!\big(i_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n})\big),\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{2}^{\,n}=g_{2n}\!\big(i_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n}),\,j_{n}(\mathsf{W}^{\,n})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\!\left[d(\mathsf{W}^{\,n},\,\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{1}^{\,n})\right]\leq D(R_{1})+\varepsilon_{n},\qquad\limsup_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\!\left[d(\mathsf{W}^{\,n},\,\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{2}^{\,n})\right]\leq D(R_{2})+\varepsilon_{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\!\left[d(\mathsf{W}^{\,n},\,\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{1}^{\,n})\right]\leq D(R_{1})+\varepsilon_{n},\qquad\limsup_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\!\left[d(\mathsf{W}^{\,n},\,\widehat{\mathsf{W}}_{2}^{\,n})\right]\leq D(R_{2})+\varepsilon_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{n}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{n}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(R)</annotation></semantics></math> is the distortion–rate function. Then,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}=R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{1},\qquad R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})-R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}=R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{1},\qquad R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})-R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence the total rate satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{total}}=R_{1}+R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})+\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">total</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{total}}=R_{1}+R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})+\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are vanishing terms such that <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> are theoretical rate–distortion limits, whereas
<math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2|1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2|1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math> are empirical operational rates
of the actual coding scheme. Here, the rate in stages matches the single-shot rate required to achieve distortion <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, encoding in two stages (first at rate <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and then refining by an additional <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2|1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2|1}</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves the same operational point as single-shot encoding at rate <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, with no rate penalty. More formally, the point <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{1},R_{2})=(R(D_{1}),R(D_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{1},R_{2})=(R(D_{1}),R(D_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> is asymptotically achievable by a two-stage description in which
the second stage refines the first. Generally, a problem defined by a source distribution <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathsf{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathsf{w})</annotation></semantics></math> and distortion measure <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(w,\widehat{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(w,\widehat{w})</annotation></semantics></math>
is said to be successively refinable,
if successive refinement from distortion <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
is achievable for every <math id="Thmdefinition1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}\geq D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}\geq D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we show that Gaussian sources are successively refinable.
We first recall the single-source construction in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Successive Refinability of Gaussian Sources). ‣ Successive Refinement. ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Foundations and Successive Refinement ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and then note that the argument extends immediately to any finite collection of independent Gaussian sources. We include these explanations explicitly to facilitate the reader in following the procedures and proofs in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Successive Refinability of Gaussian Sources)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Equitz, 1989</a><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span></cite><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">

A Gaussian source
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>
under the mean squared error (MSE) distortion measure
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(w,\widehat{w})=(w-\widehat{w})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(w,\widehat{w})=(w-\widehat{w})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
is successively refinable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Because the Gaussian source achieve its rate-distortion
function by a single-letter test channel, the <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-block
problem separates into <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independent scalar problems.
For notational clarity, we therefore work with the
single-letter random variables
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{w}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The superscripts denote refinement stages.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The Gaussian rate-distortion function is</p>
<table id="A5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D)=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma^{2}}{D},\qquad 0&lt;D\leq\sigma^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D)=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma^{2}}{D},\qquad 0&lt;D\leq\sigma^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Following Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Successive Refinability of General Sources). ‣ Successive Refinement. ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Foundations and Successive Refinement ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for any distortion pair <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist encoding functions satisfying</p>
<table id="A5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}=R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{1},\qquad R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})-R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}=R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{1},\qquad R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})-R(D_{1})+\varepsilon_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and hence a total rate</p>
<table id="A5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{total}}=R_{1}+R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})+\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>total</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{total}}=R_{1}+R_{2|1}=R(D_{2})+\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1},\varepsilon_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> vanish as <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The scalar Gaussian test channel induces the Markov chain</p>
<table id="A5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\mathsf{w}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝗐</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\mathsf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which ensures that each refinement layer depends only on its predecessor.
Furthermore, the additive Gaussian construction satisfies</p>
<table id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathsf{w};\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)})=R(D_{1}),\qquad I(\mathsf{w};\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)})=R(D_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathsf{w};\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)})=R(D_{1}),\qquad I(\mathsf{w};\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}^{(2)})=R(D_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, the achievable region coincides exactly with the single-shot
rate-distortion limits.
In other words, no additional rate is required when encoding the
Gaussian source in successive refinement stages compared to encoding
it once at distortion <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This establishes that Gaussian sources under MSE distortion are
successively refinable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gaussian Test Channel Construction.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, Equitz and Cover considered a single Gaussian source
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{w}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, we present the same construction for the case of two independent Gaussian sources, which are representative of an i.i.d. (independent and identically distributed) Gaussian vector source.</p>
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{w}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{i}^{2}),\qquad i\in\{1,2\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{w}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{i}^{2}),\qquad i\in\{1,2\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The superscripts denote refinement stages, while the subscripts denote source components.
Let the corresponding distortion levels satisfy</p>
<table id="A5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{(0)}=\sigma_{i}^{2}&gt;D_{i}^{(1)}&gt;D_{i}^{(2)}&gt;D_{i}^{(3)}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{(0)}=\sigma_{i}^{2}&gt;D_{i}^{(1)}&gt;D_{i}^{(2)}&gt;D_{i}^{(3)}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define mutually independent Gaussian increments for each <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(0)}-D_{i}^{(1)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(0)}-D_{i}^{(1)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex14Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex14Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(2)}-D_{i}^{(3)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(2)}-D_{i}^{(3)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex14Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(3)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(3)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The successive refinements are constructed as</p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex15X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex15Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(0)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(0)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex15Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex15Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(3)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(3)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex15Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{w}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{w}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(3)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}.\qquad\text{(final test channel)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mtext>(final test channel)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(3)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}.\qquad\text{(final test channel)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By construction, the distortions satisfy</p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)^{2}\right]=D_{i}^{(k)},\qquad k=1,2,3." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)^{2}\right]=D_{i}^{(k)},\qquad k=1,2,3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In vector form, let
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}=(\mathsf{w}_{1},\mathsf{w}_{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}=(\mathsf{w}_{1},\mathsf{w}_{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(k)}=(\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{1}^{(k)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{2}^{(k)})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(k)}=(\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{1}^{(k)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{2}^{(k)})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}^{(k)}=\mathrm{diag}(D_{1}^{(k)},D_{2}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}^{(k)}=\mathrm{diag}(D_{1}^{(k)},D_{2}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}+\bm{\mathsf{z}},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(\bm{0},\,\bm{D}^{(3)}\big),\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}\perp\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝘇</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝘇</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝘇</mi><mo>⟂</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}+\bm{\mathsf{z}},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(\bm{0},\,\bm{D}^{(3)}\big),\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}\perp\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">with successive refinements</p>
<table id="A5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j)}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j-1)}+\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(\bm{0},\,\bm{D}^{(j-1)}-\bm{D}^{(j)}\big),\quad j=1,2,3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝘇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝘇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j)}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j-1)}+\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(\bm{0},\,\bm{D}^{(j-1)}-\bm{D}^{(j)}\big),\quad j=1,2,3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)}\perp\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j-1)},\qquad j=1,2,3." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘇</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>⟂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{z}}^{(j)}\perp\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(j-1)},\qquad j=1,2,3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Hence, the Markov chain essential for successive refinability holds:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}\;\rightarrow\;\bm{\mathsf{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝘄</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}^{(3)}\;\rightarrow\;\bm{\mathsf{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Achievable and Refinement Rates.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The achievable rates for each stage are given by:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex21X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(1)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex21Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex21Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{i}^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{i}^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(3)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(3)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the two-source vector:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R^{(k)}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(k)}},\qquad k=1,2,3." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(k)}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(k)}},\qquad k=1,2,3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The incremental (refinement) rates satisfy</p>
<table id="A5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R^{(k)}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(k-1)}}{D_{i}^{(k)}},\qquad D_{i}^{(0)}=\sigma_{i}^{2},\qquad R^{(k)}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}\Delta R^{(j)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R^{(k)}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(k-1)}}{D_{i}^{(k)}},\qquad D_{i}^{(0)}=\sigma_{i}^{2},\qquad R^{(k)}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}\Delta R^{(j)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The incremental refinement rate derivation can be written as follows. For each component <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the incremental mutual information between successive reconstructions, where the mean squared distortion at stage <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[d\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)^{2}\right]=D_{i}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.350em;" width="0.350em"><mi>d</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[d\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(k)}\big)^{2}\right]=D_{i}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Using this distortion characterization, the incremental mutual information between successive reconstructions is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex25X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\,\big|\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\,\big|\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)})-h(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)})-h(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex25Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\log(2\pi e\,D_{i}^{(1)})-\tfrac{1}{2}\log(2\pi e\,D_{i}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\log(2\pi e\,D_{i}^{(1)})-\tfrac{1}{2}\log(2\pi e\,D_{i}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex25Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, the incremental (refinement) rate for component <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\,\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\,\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Summing over both components yields</p>
<table id="A5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\,\Delta R^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}=R^{(2)}-R^{(1)}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\,\Delta R^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}=R^{(2)}-R^{(1)}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Single-Shot Encoding Equivalence.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If we encode directly to the finer distortion level <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., skipping the first stage), the Gaussian rate–distortion function gives</p>
<table id="A5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\text{direct}}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>direct</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\text{direct}}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Adding the two refinement stages, however,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(1)}+\Delta R^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\Big[\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}+\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\Big]=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}=R_{\text{direct}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>direct</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(1)}+\Delta R^{(2)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\Big[\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}+\log\!\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\Big]=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{2}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}=R_{\text{direct}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, the total rate of the two-stage successive refinement scheme matches exactly the single-shot rate–distortion function:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\,R^{(1)}+\Delta R^{(2)}=R(D^{(2)})\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\,R^{(1)}+\Delta R^{(2)}=R(D^{(2)})\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, there is no rate penalty for successive refinement. By the nested reconstruction structure, the variables satisfy the Markov chain</p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\mathsf{w}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\;\rightarrow\;\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\;\rightarrow\;\mathsf{w}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\,\big|\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)=h\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)-h\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗐</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)}\,\big|\,\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)=h\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)-h\!\big(\mathsf{w}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{w}}_{i}^{(2)}\big)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">confirming the Markov consistency condition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Extension to i.i.d. Gaussian Vectors.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a memoryless vector Gaussian source
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}=(\mathsf{w}_{1},\ldots,\mathsf{w}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}=(\mathsf{w}_{1},\ldots,\mathsf{w}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>
with independent components
<math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{w}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{i}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{w}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{i}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the rate-distortion function decomposes additively:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\log\!\frac{\sigma_{i}^{2}}{D_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since each scalar component is successively refinable under MSE distortion,
their independent combination is also successively refinable with total rate equal to the sum of per-component rates.
Hence, i.i.d. Gaussian vector sources are likewise successively refinable.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proofs of Auxiliary Results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Having established that i.i.d. Gaussian sources are successively refinable under the
standard MSE distortion, we now ask whether this property extends to weighted
distortions. The following results help establish Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Correlated Gaussian under MSE is successively refinable). ‣ F.2 Successive Refinability under WMSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sakrison (1968)</a></cite> proved the rate-distortion function for
continuous-time Gaussian processes under a weighted square error criterion.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover &amp; Thomas (2006, Ch. 10)</a></cite> covers Gaussian rate-distortion theory and the
reverse water-filling solution approach to solve
the rate-distortion problem for parallel Gaussian sources. The following
theorem adapts these results to the discrete, finite-dimensional matrix setting,
replacing the Karhunen-Loève expansion with a finite eigen-decomposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(WMSE Rate-Distortion Equivalence)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
be a zero-mean i.i.d. Gaussian random matrix, and let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a deterministic matrix. Consider
the weighted MSE distortion</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;\coloneqq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\,\bm{X}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;\coloneqq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\,\bm{X}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for the transformed source <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the rate-distortion function for <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mathsf{W}},d_{\mathrm{WMSE}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mathsf{W}},d_{\mathrm{WMSE}})</annotation></semantics></math>
equals the standard Gaussian MSE rate-distortion function for
<math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, there is a one-to-one correspondence
between their rate-distortion curves and optimal codebooks at every distortion
level <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in three steps. First, we reduce the WMSE problem for
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> to a standard MSE problem for a transformed source
by introducing a linear change of variables. Second, we diagonalize the
covariance of the transformed source via eigen-decomposition to obtain
independent scalar Gaussian components, and apply reverse water-filling to
solve the resulting rate-distortion problem. Third, we pull the optimal
reconstruction back to <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> by inverting the change of
variables, treating each structural case of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> separately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout Steps 1 and 2, we work with the vectorized representations</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}\;\coloneqq\;\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}})\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\cdot d_{\mathrm{in}}},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{y}}\;\coloneqq\;\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X})\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\cdot n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}\;\coloneqq\;\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}})\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\cdot d_{\mathrm{in}}},\qquad\bm{\mathsf{y}}\;\coloneqq\;\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X})\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\cdot n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which allow us to compute the covariance structure needed for eigen-decomposition. We return to matrix form in Step 3 for the pullback.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Reduction to standard MSE.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\,\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\,\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math>
be a zero-mean i.i.d. Gaussian random vector and let
<math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a deterministic matrix. Consider the weighted mean squared error distortion (WMSE):</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{w}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{w}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}})\,\bm{X}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{w}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}})=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{w}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}})\,\bm{X}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Introduce the linear change of variables</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}\;\coloneqq\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\bm{\mathsf{w}},\qquad\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\;\coloneqq\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝘄</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}\;\coloneqq\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\bm{\mathsf{w}},\qquad\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\;\coloneqq\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kronecker product, so that</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}\!\left(\bm{\mathsf{w}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}\right)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}\!\left(\bm{\mathsf{w}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{w}}}\right)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-mean i.i.d. Gaussian with <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{w}}=\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗐</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{w}}=\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-mean Gaussian with covariance</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}\;=\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{w}}\,\bigl(\bm{X}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\;=\;\bigl(\sigma_{w}^{2}\,\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}\bigr)\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}\;=\;\bigl(\bm{X}^{\top}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\,\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{w}}\,\bigl(\bm{X}\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}\bigr)\;=\;\bigl(\sigma_{w}^{2}\,\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}\bigr)\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, coding <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math> at rate <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and distortion <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>
is equivalent to coding <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> under standard MSE at the same rate and distortion. It, therefore, suffices to solve the standard Gaussian MSE problem for <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Eigen-decomposition and reverse water-filling.</span>
However, since <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a correlated Gaussian vector, we cannot apply
water-filling directly. The eigen-decomposition of <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>
rotates into a basis of independent scalar Gaussians, to which the classical
reverse water-filling solution applies. Let</p>
<table id="A6.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}=\bm{U}\,\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots)\,\bm{U}^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}=\bm{U}\,\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots)\,\bm{U}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">be the eigen-decomposition of the covariance of <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expanding in this orthonormal basis,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\sum_{i}\mathsf{y}_{i}\,\bm{u}_{i},\qquad\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}=\sum_{i}\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}\,\bm{u}_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\sum_{i}\mathsf{y}_{i}\,\bm{u}_{i},\qquad\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}=\sum_{i}\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}\,\bm{u}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">where the scalar coefficients <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent Gaussians with
variances <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal test channel for each scalar component is additive Gaussian with a refinement <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{y}}_{i}=\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}+\mathsf{z}_{i},\qquad\mathsf{z}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,D_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{y}}_{i}=\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}+\mathsf{z}_{i},\qquad\mathsf{z}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,D_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p">achieving per-component distortion <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthonormal, the <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm is preserved under
the change of basis, and the total distortion decomposes as a sum over components,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{WMSE}}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mathsf{y}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i})^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}D_{i},\qquad D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{WMSE}}=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}\mathbb{E}\!\left[(\mathsf{y}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i})^{2}\right]=\sum_{i}D_{i},\qquad D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly the total rate decomposes as a sum of scalar rates. The
rate-distortion function for <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> under MSE is therefore</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D)\;=\;\min_{D_{i}}\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}}\right),\qquad\text{subject to }0\leq D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i},\quad\sum_{i}D_{i}\leq D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>subject to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D)\;=\;\min_{D_{i}}\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}}\right),\qquad\text{subject to }0\leq D_{i}\leq\lambda_{i},\quad\sum_{i}D_{i}\leq D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">This constrained minimization is solved by reverse water-filling, as illustrated
in Figure <a href="#A6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ F.1 Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Imagine
pouring water up to a level <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> over a landscape where each coordinate
<math id="A6.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has height <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal per-component distortion is <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=\min(\mu,\lambda_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=\min(\mu,\lambda_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math> where the water level <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}D_{i}=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}D_{i}=D</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives
two regimes for each component:</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Below the water level</span> (<math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math>): the component
is fully submerged, so <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and no rate is allocated. The
source is too weak to be worth encoding.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Above the water level</span> (<math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math>): the component
is only partially submerged, so <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and rate is allocated
proportional to <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log_{2}(\lambda_{i}/\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_{2}(\lambda_{i}/\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>. The stronger the source,
the more bits it receives.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A6.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">The total distortion includes contributions from both active and inactive
components,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D\;=\;\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}\leq\mu}\lambda_{i}\;+\;\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\mu," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\;=\;\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}\leq\mu}\lambda_{i}\;+\;\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\mu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">while only the active components <math id="A6.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i:\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i:\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu\}</annotation></semantics></math> contribute to
the rate,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(D)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\mu}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\mu}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.F10.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="213.11" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 307.42 213.11" width="307.42"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,213.11) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(23.74,0) translate(0,18.42)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fg-color:#E6E6FF;" color="#E6E6FF" fill="#E6E6FF" stroke="#E6E6FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 88.58 L 23.62 88.58 L 23.62 0 Z M 23.62 88.58"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3FF;" color="#B3B3FF" fill="#B3B3FF" stroke="#B3B3FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 78.74 M 0 78.74 L 0 88.58 L 23.62 88.58 L 23.62 78.74 Z M 23.62 88.58"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 78.74 L 23.62 78.74 L 23.62 0 Z M 23.62 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fill-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fg-color:#6666FF;" color="#6666FF" fill="#6666FF" stroke="#6666FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 88.58 L 23.62 88.58 L 23.62 0 Z M 23.62 88.58"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.35 -13.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F10.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fill-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" color="#3333FF" fill="#3333FF" stroke="#3333FF" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.67 95.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="14.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F10.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fg-color:#E6E6FF;" color="#E6E6FF" fill="#E6E6FF" stroke="#E6E6FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 31.5 0 M 31.5 0 L 31.5 127.95 L 55.12 127.95 L 55.12 0 Z M 55.12 127.95"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3FF;" color="#B3B3FF" fill="#B3B3FF" stroke="#B3B3FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 31.5 78.74 M 31.5 78.74 L 31.5 127.95 L 55.12 127.95 L 55.12 78.74 Z M 55.12 127.95"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 31.5 0 M 31.5 0 L 31.5 78.74 L 55.12 78.74 L 55.12 0 Z M 55.12 78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fill-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fg-color:#6666FF;" color="#6666FF" fill="#6666FF" stroke="#6666FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 31.5 0 M 31.5 0 L 31.5 127.95 L 55.12 127.95 L 55.12 0 Z M 55.12 127.95"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 39.85 -13.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F10.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fill-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" color="#3333FF" fill="#3333FF" stroke="#3333FF" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 36.17 134.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="14.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F10.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 62.99 0 M 62.99 0 L 62.99 59.06 L 86.61 59.06 L 86.61 0 Z M 86.61 59.06"></path></g><defs><pattern height="4" id="pgfpat3" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" width="4"><symbol id="pgfsym3"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 4.29 4.29"></path></g><g></g><defs><pattern id="pgfupat19" href="#pgfpat3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#008000;--ltx-fill-color:#008000;" fill="#008000" 