ate:  <math id="A6.F10.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\log_{2}(\lambda_{i}/\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\log_{2}(\lambda_{i}/\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 177.17 15.75 M 177.17 15.75 L 177.17 31.5 L 196.85 31.5 L 196.85 15.75 Z M 196.85 31.5"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900"><path style="fill:none" d="M 177.17 15.75 M 177.17 15.75 L 177.17 31.5 L 196.85 31.5 L 196.85 15.75 Z M 196.85 31.5"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 203.71 20.16)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="207.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.F10.pic2.2" class="ltx_text">Distortion:  <math id="A6.F10.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>  (active),  <math id="A6.F10.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>  (inactive)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 39.37 -7.87 M 39.37 -7.87 L 39.37 7.87 L 59.06 7.87 L 59.06 -7.87 Z M 59.06 7.87"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 39.37 -7.87 M 39.37 -7.87 L 39.37 7.87 L 59.06 7.87 L 59.06 -7.87 Z M 59.06 7.87"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 65.91 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.72em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="51.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.F10.pic2.3" class="ltx_text">Active:  <math id="A6.F10.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 177.17 -7.87 M 177.17 -7.87 L 177.17 7.87 L 196.85 7.87 L 196.85 -7.87 Z M 196.85 7.87"></path></g><defs><pattern id="pgfupat22" href="#pgfpat3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#008000;--ltx-fill-color:#008000;" fill="#008000" stroke="#008000"><use href="#pgfsym3"></use></g></pattern></defs><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 177.17 -7.87 M 177.17 -7.87 L 177.17 7.87 L 196.85 7.87 L 196.85 -7.87 Z M 196.85 7.87"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 177.17 -7.87 M 177.17 -7.87 L 177.17 7.87 L 196.85 7.87 L 196.85 -7.87 Z M 196.85 7.87"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 203.71 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="60.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A6.F10.pic2.4" class="ltx_text">Inactive:  <math id="A6.F10.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Reverse water-filling method</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">As the distortion budget <math id="A6.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> decreases, the water level <math id="A6.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> drops,
activating more components and allocating rate to progressively weaker
directions of <math id="A6.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Pullback to <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Since the change of variables <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}\mapsto\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝘆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}\mapsto\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is linear and invertible, the rate-distortion function derived above for
<math id="A6.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> under standard MSE is equivalently the rate-distortion
function for <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A6.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{w}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{w}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{W}})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{Y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{Y}})</annotation></semantics></math> are simply
vectorized representations of the underlying matrices, we can equivalently write</p>
<table id="A6.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}\;=\;\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X},\qquad d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}\;=\;\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X},\qquad d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">confirming that the distortion equivalence holds in matrix form as well.
The optimal codebook for <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> is then recovered from the
optimal <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by inverting the relation
<math id="A6.SS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose precise
form depends on the structure of <math id="A6.SS1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and is treated separately
in each of the three cases below.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 1</span>: <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is square and invertible (<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}=n</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore</p>
<table id="A6.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 2</span>: <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is tall and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible (<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{+}=(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{+}=(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the left inverse of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, which
satisfies <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{+}\bm{X}=\bm{I}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{+}\bm{X}=\bm{I}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}\;=\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,(\bm{X}^{+}\bm{X})\;=\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}\;=\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,(\bm{X}^{+}\bm{X})\;=\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A6.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 3</span>: <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is wide and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> invertible (<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}=\bm{U}_{d}\,\bm{S}_{d}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}=\bm{U}_{d}\,\bm{S}_{d}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the compact singular value decomposition (SVD) of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A6.Ex52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex52X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{U}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{U}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{is orthogonal}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>is orthogonal</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{is orthogonal},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex52Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{S}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{S}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{diag}(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{d_{\mathrm{in}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{diag}(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{d_{\mathrm{in}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xa.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex52Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{V}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{V}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52Xb.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}\bm{V}_{d}=\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{in}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}\bm{V}_{d}=\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{in}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is wide and cannot be inverted directly, we introduce
the square, invertible surrogate</p>
<table id="A6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{X}}:=\bm{U}_{d}\,\bm{S}_{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},\qquad\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}=\bm{S}_{d}^{-1}\bm{U}_{d}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{X}}:=\bm{U}_{d}\,\bm{S}_{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},\qquad\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}=\bm{S}_{d}^{-1}\bm{U}_{d}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so that
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}=\widetilde{\bm{X}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}=\widetilde{\bm{X}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math> Rather than working with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which inherits the non-invertibility
of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead work with the compressed surrogate</p>
<table id="A6.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\;\coloneqq\;\bm{\mathsf{W}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\;\coloneqq\;\bm{\mathsf{W}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}=\widetilde{\bm{X}}\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}=\widetilde{\bm{X}}\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, the original outputs are recovered as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}=\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}=\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">and since <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> has orthonormal columns, right multiplication
by <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the Frobenius norm, giving</p>
<table id="A6.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">It therefore suffices to solve the rate-distortion problem for
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
square and invertible, this reduces to Case 1, and the same reverse
water-filling applied to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the
optimal reconstruction <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The reconstruction <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is then recovered via</p>
<table id="A6.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\;=\;\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\;=\;\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">To verify that this achieves the correct distortion on the original samples,
note that the forward map gives
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}=\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}=\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the output error satisfies
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}=(\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}})\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}=(\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}})\,\bm{V}_{d}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the norm equivalence established above, we conclude</p>
<table id="A6.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}-\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In all three cases, the recovery <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
constructed so that</p>
<table id="A6.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|(\bm{\mathsf{W}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\bm{X}\|_{F}^{2}\right]\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\|_{F}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">confirming that the WMSE distortion on <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> equals the
standard MSE distortion on <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> in all cases.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, this theorem shows:</p>
<ol id="A6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Distortion equivalence.</span> For any reconstruction
<math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, setting
<math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A6.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}(\bm{\mathsf{W}},\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\|\bm{\mathsf{Y}}-\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\bigr\|_{F}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rate-distortion equivalence.</span> The rate-distortion function
for <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\mathsf{W}},d_{\mathrm{WMSE}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\mathsf{W}},d_{\mathrm{WMSE}})</annotation></semantics></math> equals the standard
Gaussian MSE rate-distortion function for <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, given
by reverse water-filling over the eigenvalues <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of
<math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(D)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\mu}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i\,:\,\lambda_{i}&gt;\mu}\log_{2}\!\left(\frac{\lambda_{i}}{\mu}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\min(\mu,\lambda_{i})=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\min(\mu,\lambda_{i})=D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Codebook recovery.</span> The optimal reconstruction
<math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is recovered from the optimal
<math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by inverting
<math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝗪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{Y}}=\bm{\mathsf{W}}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The precise form depends on the structure of <math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Square</span> (<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}=n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> invertible<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext=")" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">)</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,\bm{X}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tall</span> (<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math>
invertible<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext=")" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">)</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}\,(\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})^{-1}\bm{X}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wide</span> (<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{in}}&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>, via compact SVD
<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}=\bm{U}_{d}\bm{S}_{d}\bm{V}_{d}^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}=\bm{U}_{d}\bm{S}_{d}\bm{V}_{d}^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗬</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{W}}}=\widehat{\widetilde{\bm{\mathsf{Y}}}}\,\widetilde{\bm{X}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A6.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{X}}\coloneqq\bm{U}_{d}\bm{S}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{X}}\coloneqq\bm{U}_{d}\bm{S}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Successive Refinability under WMSE</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (WMSE Rate-Distortion Equivalence). ‣ F.1 Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> established the rate-distortion equivalence
at a single operating point <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R(D),D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R(D),D)</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show this equivalence
holds simultaneously across all nested distortion levels <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;D_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;D_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, This means the one-shot encoding at any distortion
level <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the same rate as <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-stage refinement, with no
rate penalty. Therefore, a single embedded bitstream suffices in place
of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent codes.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Correlated Gaussian under MSE is successively refinable)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setting of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (WMSE Rate-Distortion Equivalence). ‣ F.1 Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the source
<math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> is successively refinable under
<math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, for any nested distortion levels
<math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;D_{K}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}&gt;D_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;D_{K}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a single embedded
bitstream whose <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th prefix achieves the optimal rate-distortion
pair <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R(D_{k}),D_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R(D_{k}),D_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>WMSE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{WMSE}}</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously for
all <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, at the same total rate as <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent codes each
optimally designed for its own distortion level.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in two steps. First, we show that
<math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{Y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}=\operatorname{vec}(\bm{\mathsf{Y}})</annotation></semantics></math>
is successively refinable under standard MSE by constructing nested
test channels that achieve each <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R(D_{k}),D_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R(D_{k}),D_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> with no rate penalty.
Second, we lift this result to <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> via the
distortion equivalence of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (WMSE Rate-Distortion Equivalence). ‣ F.1 Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Successive refinability of
<math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> under MSE.</span>
By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (WMSE Rate-Distortion Equivalence). ‣ F.1 Rate-Distortion Under Weighted MSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-mean
Gaussian with covariance <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}=(\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}=(\sigma_{w}^{2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{X})\otimes\bm{I}_{d_{\mathrm{out}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="A6.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}\;=\;\bm{U}\,\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots)\,\bm{U}^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝗒</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\mathsf{y}}\;=\;\bm{U}\,\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\ldots)\,\bm{U}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">be its eigen-decomposition, yielding independent scalar Gaussian
components <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{y}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\lambda_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{y}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\lambda_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the
components are independent, it suffices to show successive
refinability for each scalar <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> separately, then sum
over components.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scalar test channel construction.</span>
For each component <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, superscripts denote the refinement
stage, while subscripts index the
source component. For example, <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reconstruction of
component <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> after stage <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
Gaussian increment added at stage <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Define nested distortion levels <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{(1)}&gt;D_{i}^{(2)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{(1)}&gt;D_{i}^{(2)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, define mutually independent Gaussian increments</p>
<table id="A6.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\lambda_{i}-D_{i}^{(1)}\right),\quad\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)}\right),\quad\mathsf{z}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(2)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,\lambda_{i}-D_{i}^{(1)}\right),\quad\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)}\right),\quad\mathsf{z}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\left(0,\,D_{i}^{(2)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and construct successive reconstructions</p>
<table id="A6.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(0)}\;=\;0,\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(0)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)},\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)},\qquad\mathsf{y}_{i}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(0)}\;=\;0,\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(0)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)},\qquad\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)},\qquad\mathsf{y}_{i}\;=\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}+\mathsf{z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Each stage <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> refines the previous estimate by adding an
independent Gaussian increment of variance <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{(k-1)}-D_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{(k-1)}-D_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By construction, <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\mathsf{y}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(k)})^{2}\bigr]=D_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[(\mathsf{y}_{i}-\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(k)})^{2}\bigr]=D_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>,
and since the increments are mutually independent the Markov chain holds by construction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Equitz, 1989</a>)</cite>.</p>
<table id="A6.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\;\to\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\;\to\;\mathsf{y}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\;\to\;\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\;\to\;\mathsf{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">No rate penalty.</span>
The rate <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the rate needed to encode
<math id="A6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the information required to describe the
first-stage reconstruction <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> from
scratch. The rate <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the additional rate needed to
encode <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝗓</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{z}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the new information required to
describe how the reconstruction improves from
<math id="A6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Formally,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}\;=\;I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}\;=\;I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(1)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A6.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\,\middle|\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)\;=\;h\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)-h\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\right)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\,\middle|\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)\;=\;h\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\right)-h\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i}\mid\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)},\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\right)\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The total two-stage rate equals to the one-shot rate at
<math id="A6.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}+\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}+\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\;=\;R_{i}(D_{i}^{(2)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R_{i}^{(1)}+\Delta R_{i}^{(2)}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(1)}}+\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{D_{i}^{(1)}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\lambda_{i}}{D_{i}^{(2)}}\;=\;R_{i}(D_{i}^{(2)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">confirming no rate penalty for the <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component. The Markov
consistency condition</p>
<table id="A6.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\,\middle|\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\right)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝗒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\!\left(\mathsf{y}_{i};\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}\,\middle|\,\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">holds since <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of
<math id="A6.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗒</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{y}}_{i}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> under the nested construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The same construction extends to <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> stages by defining <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>
independent increments of variances <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}-D_{i}^{(1)},\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)},\,\ldots,\,D_{i}^{(K-1)}-D_{i}^{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}-D_{i}^{(1)},\,D_{i}^{(1)}-D_{i}^{(2)},\,\ldots,\,D_{i}^{(K-1)}-D_{i}^{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the joint Markov chain</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(1)}\;\to\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(2)}\;\to\;\cdots\;\to\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(K)}\;\to\;\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝘆</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝘆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(1)}\;\to\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(2)}\;\to\;\cdots\;\to\;\widehat{\bm{\mathsf{y}}}^{(K)}\;\to\;\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds since the scalar Markov chains hold independently for each
component, with each stage being a strictly finer approximation of
<math id="A6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> than the previous. Moreover, Figures <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Proof. ‣ F.2 Successive Refinability under WMSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <a href="#A6.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ F.2 Successive Refinability under WMSE ‣ Appendix F Proofs of Auxiliary Results ‣ Multi-Bitwidth Quantization for LLMs Using Additive Codebooks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> illustrate the
three possible activation patterns: at the first stage, case (a) starts with only one component active while the other remains inactive, case (b) starts with both components already active, and case (c) starts with both components inactive. In all cases the <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math>
brackets confirm that the incremental rate at each stage equals
exactly <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(D_{k+1})-R(D_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(D_{k+1})-R(D_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mathsf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝘆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mathsf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
successively refinable under MSE.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A6.F11.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.F11.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="258.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 150.79 258.66" width="150.79"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,258.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(32.9,0) translate(0,45.27)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6FF;--ltx-fg-color:#E6E6FF;" color="#E6E6FF" fill="#E6E6FF" stroke="#E6E6FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 162.4 L 35.43 162.4 L 35.43 0 Z M 35.43 162.4"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fill-color:#B3B3FF;--ltx-fg-color:#B3B3FF;" color="#B3B3FF" fill="#B3B3FF" stroke="#B3B3FF"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 103.35 M 0 103.35 L 0 162.4 L 35.43 162.4 L 35.43 103.35 Z M 35.43 162.4"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 103.35 L 35.43 103.35 L 35.43 0 Z M 35.43 103.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fill-color:#6666FF;--ltx-fg-color:#6666FF;" color="#6666FF" fill="#6666FF" stroke="#6666FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 M 0 0 L 0 162.4 L 35.43 162.4 L 35.43 0 Z M 35.43 162.4"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.26 -13.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fill-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" color="#3333FF" fill="#3333FF" stroke="#3333FF" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.58 169.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="14.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" mathcolor="#3333FF">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fill-color:#CCFFCC;--ltx-fg-color:#CCFFCC;" color="#CCFFCC" fill="#CCFFCC" stroke="#CCFFCC"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 53.15 0 M 53.15 0 L 53.15 73.82 L 88.58 73.82 L 88.58 0 Z M 88.58 73.82"></path></g><defs><pattern id="pgfupat23" href="#pgfpat3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#008000;--ltx-fill-color:#008000;" fill="#008000" stroke="#008000"><use href="#pgfsym3"></use></g></pattern></defs><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 53.15 0 M 53.15 0 L 53.15 73.82 L 88.58 73.82 L 88.58 0 Z M 88.58 73.82"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 53.15 0 M 53.15 0 L 53.15 73.82 L 88.58 73.82 L 88.58 0 Z M 88.58 73.82"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 67.41 -13.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#008000;--ltx-fill-color:#008000;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;" color="#008000" fill="#008000" stroke="#008000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 63.73 80.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="14.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;" mathcolor="#008000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;" mathcolor="#008000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B30000;--ltx-fill-color:#B30000;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;" color="#B30000" fill="#B30000" stroke="#B30000" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -8.86 103.35 L 97.44 103.35"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#B30000;--ltx-fill-color:#B30000;--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;" color="#B30000" fill="#B30000" stroke="#B30000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -28.29 101.71)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:1.05em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" color="#000000" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="14.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;" mathcolor="#B30000">μ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;" mathcolor="#B30000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -8.86 0 L -8.86 190.95"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -8.86 190.95)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -15.2 199.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="12.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A6.F11.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -8.86 0 L 102.36 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.64pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 102.36 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.16 2.88 C -1.98 1.8 0 0.18 0.54 0 C 0 -0.18 -1.98 -1.8 -2.16 -2.88"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 108.51 -4.56)"><f